{"chapter-slug":"rw8-25 KH","paragraph":971,"wording":"[Bandit]","event":"named","holder-quote":"Leprel was pulling at her hair, although it occurred to her that if Yvlon had taken the Champion’s hand, she and Rexel would have been left behind.","id":"172af4fa-373b-5af1-94bc-e61303bb61cb"}
{"chapter-slug":"rwInterlude - Pisces (Revised)","paragraph":61,"wording":"[Bandit]","event":"named","holder-quote":"The man was a pompous, ruthless lowlife, and Pisces would have happily called him a [Bandit] wearing a [Merchant]’s skin if he were freed. He detested Igheriz, but unlike Yvlon—or Ceria come to that—Pisces could lie and be polite. So he smiled.","id":"420a7648-ca7c-5191-9a8c-2917a6175234"}
